{{see also|New York's 4th congressional district}}
The 4th district is based on the South Shore of Nassau County and is entirely within the town of Hempstead. The district was mostly unchanged by redistricting. It had a PVI of D+5 and voted for Joe Biden by 15 points in 2020. The incumbent was Democrat [[Kathleen Rice]], who was reelected with 56.1% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=results/> On February 15, 2022, Rice announced that she would retire at the end of her term.<ref name="Rice">{{#invoke:cite|news|last=Rogers |first=Alex |date=February 15, 2022 |title=Kathleen Rice becomes 30th House Democrat to not seek reelection in 2022 |work=CNN |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2022/02/15/politics/kathleen-rice-not-running-congress/index.html |access-date=February 15, 2022}}</ref>

