{{see also|New York's 5th congressional district}}
The 5th district is based in Southeast Queens, including the neighborhoods of Jamaica, Hollis, Laurelton, Richmond Hill, Ozone Park, Howard Beach, and the Rockaways. The district was mostly unchanged by redistricting. It had a PVI of D+32 and voted for Joe Biden by 63 points in 2020. The incumbent was Democrat [[Gregory Meeks]], who was reelected unopposed with 99.3% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=results/>

