{{see also|New York's 9th congressional district}}
The 9th district is based in South and Central Brooklyn, including the neighborhoods of Prospect Heights, Crown Heights, Midwood, and Borough Park. The district was mostly unchanged by redistricting. It had a PVI of D+27 and voted for Joe Biden by 52 points in 2020. The incumbent was Democrat [[Yvette Clarke]], who was reelected with 83% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=results/>

