{{see also|New York's 11th congressional district}}
The 11th district includes all of Staten Island and the neighborhoods of Bay Ridge, Fort Hamilton, Dyker Heights, Bath Beach, and Bensonhurst in Brooklyn. The seat was mostly unchanged by redistricting. It had a PVI of R+5 and voted for Donald Trump by 8 points in 2020, making it the only Republican-leaning district in New York City. The incumbent was Republican [[Nicole Malliotakis]], who was elected with 53% of the vote in 2020 over then-incumbent [[Max Rose]], who ran again for his former seat, but lost by a landslide margin of 23.5%.<ref name=results/><ref name=":3" />

