{{see also|New York's 20th congressional district}}
The 20th district is based in the Capital Region, including Albany, Troy, Schenectady, and Saratoga Springs. It includes all of Albany, Schenectady, and Saratoga counties and parts of Rensselaer County. Due to redistricting, the district lost Amsterdam to the 21st district. It had a PVI of D+7 and voted for Joe Biden by 20 points in 2020. The incumbent was Democrat [[Paul Tonko]], who was reelected with 61.2% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=results/>

