{{see also|New York's 21st congressional district}}
The 21st district is based in [[upstate New York]] encompassing the [[Adirondack Mountains]] and [[North Country (New York)|North Country]] regions. Also including [[Glens Falls, New York|Glens Falls]], [[Lake George (New York)|Lake George]], [[Plattsburgh, New York|Plattsburgh]], [[Potsdam, New York|Potsdam]], [[Amsterdam, New York|Amsterdam]], and [[Cooperstown, New York|Cooperstown]]. Redistricting added parts of the [[Mohawk Valley]] to the district while removing [[Watertown, New York|Watertown]]. The district had a [[Cook Partisan Voting Index|PVI]] of R+9 and voted for Donald Trump by 12 points in 2020. The incumbent was Republican [[Elise Stefanik]], who was reelected with 58.8% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=results/>

===Republican nominee===
